<speak>It began with a drawer that would not close properly. I thought there must be something caught at the back, but really it was just too full. I took everything out and found appliance manuals for things we no longer owned, old appointment cards, and envelopes I had kept because I might need them. After that, I looked at the other drawers. I realised my system was less a system and more a series of places where paper had landed.</speak>